        <updated>2026-07-28T00:00:00.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img alt="" loading="lazy" id="w-node-_2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63771-83c22e73" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6a6875977f6cc1eaeb68b226_once%20case%20cover.png" sizes="100vw" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6a6875977f6cc1eaeb68b226_once%20case%20cover-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6a6875977f6cc1eaeb68b226_once%20case%20cover-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6a6875977f6cc1eaeb68b226_once%20case%20cover-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6a6875977f6cc1eaeb68b226_once%20case%20cover.png 1200w" class="post-image"><div class="post-content-div"><div class="div-block-992"><div class="div-block-1010"><div fs-list-field="category" class="blog-category">AI Detection &amp; Response</div><div class="highlight-tag pop w-condition-invisible">Popular</div><div class="highlight-tag w-condition-invisible">Highlights</div><div class="hide w-dyn-list"><div role="list" class="w-dyn-items"><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">AI SOC</div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">CDR</div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">SOAR</div></div></div></div></div><a data-wf-native-id-path="2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63775_instance-2" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63775" data-wf-cms-context="%5B%7B%22collectionId%22%3A%2265dbcab8c88303f083c22dc7%22%2C%22itemId%22%3A%226a68738efe5b39ccd0bc6f92%22%7D%5D" href="/post/one-case-not-a-swarm-organizing-the-ai-soc" class="b-title w-inline-block"><h2 fs-list-field="title" class="heading-29 blog">One Case, Not a Swarm: Organizing the AI SOC</h2><div class="blog-par limit-char">One attack in Part 2 threw off four separate alerts, and the obvious fix, one investigation agent per alert, rebuilds every failure of the overloaded human SOC at machine speed and cost. Part 3 of the Building the Agentic SOC series lays out the alternative: every related alert attaches to one linked case, worked by a small set of specialized agents, a dispatcher and case leader, over one shared model of the case and the environment.</div></a></div><div class="divider-full space small"></div><div class="div-block-773"><div class="writer-small dark"><img height="70" width="70" alt="Petr Zuzanov" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23).png" sizes="70px" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23)-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23)-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23).png 1400w" class="writer-image-small"><div><div fs-list-field="author" class="writer---blog-page-home">Petr Zuzanov</div></div></div><div class="div-block-790 xs"><div class="div-block-953"><div class="writer---blog-page-home date">Jul 28, 2026</div></div><div class="code-embed-3 w-embed"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
