        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img alt="" loading="lazy" id="w-node-_2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63771-83c22e73" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69f9a94ee72a1a5569b51e5b_Model%20of%20Reality-1.png" sizes="100vw" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69f9a94ee72a1a5569b51e5b_Model%20of%20Reality-1-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69f9a94ee72a1a5569b51e5b_Model%20of%20Reality-1-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69f9a94ee72a1a5569b51e5b_Model%20of%20Reality-1-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69f9a94ee72a1a5569b51e5b_Model%20of%20Reality-1.png 1200w" class="post-image"><div class="post-content-div"><div class="div-block-992"><div class="div-block-1010"><div fs-list-field="category" class="blog-category">AI Detection &amp; Response</div><div class="highlight-tag pop w-condition-invisible">Popular</div><div class="highlight-tag w-condition-invisible">Highlights</div><div class="hide w-dyn-list"><div role="list" class="w-dyn-items"><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">AI SOC</div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">CDR</div></div></div></div></div><a data-wf-native-id-path="2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63775_instance-9" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63775" data-wf-cms-context="%5B%7B%22collectionId%22%3A%2265dbcab8c88303f083c22dc7%22%2C%22itemId%22%3A%2269f898836893d987b635b75f%22%7D%5D" href="/post/before-security-can-use-more-ai-it-needs-a-model-of-reality" class="b-title w-inline-block"><h2 fs-list-field="title" class="heading-29 blog">Before Security Can Use More AI, It Needs a Model of Reality</h2><div class="blog-par limit-char">AI agents and tools won't scale security until the environment itself is modeled. Real context isn't enrichment — it's a live representation of state. That shift changes what tools, harnesses, and agents actually mean, and what StreamForce is built on.</div></a></div><div class="divider-full space small"></div><div class="div-block-773"><div class="writer-small dark"><img height="70" width="70" alt="Maor Idan" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/686cf9456379ac7835bd0843_MAOR.webp" sizes="70px" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/686cf9456379ac7835bd0843_MAOR-p-500.webp 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/686cf9456379ac7835bd0843_MAOR.webp 783w" class="writer-image-small"><div><div fs-list-field="author" class="writer---blog-page-home">Maor Idan</div></div></div><div class="div-block-790 xs"><div class="div-block-953"><div class="writer---blog-page-home date">May 6, 2026</div></div><div class="code-embed-3 w-embed"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
